\\ell_X,\\ell_Z) \\sim D}\\\n   801\t\t\t\\E_{(x,z,\\alpha,\\beta) \\in \\ell}\n   802\t\t\t&\\sum_{f_X,f_Z} \\bra{\\hat\\psi}\n   803\t\t\t\\big(T^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}\\big)_{\\mathsf{A}\\mathsf{A}'} \\ot\n   804\t\t\t\\big(\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},Z),z}_{f_Z(z)}\n   805\t\t\t\\big)_{\\mathsf{B}\\mathsf{A}''}\n   806\t\t\t\\ket{\\hat\\psi}\\,,\n   807\t\t\\end{align*}\n   808\t\twhere $\\delta_{\\mathrm{Line}}$ is the error function of\n   809\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-comm-line-cons}.\n   810\t\\end{lemma}\n   811\t\\begin{proof}\n   812\t\t\\uses{lem:qld-comm-line-cons, lem:qld-sublines, lem:qld-xz-lines,\n   813\t\t\tlem:restricted-line-mixture-bounds, def:ith-restricted-line,\n   814\t\t\tdef:expanded-line-measurement}\n   815\t\tBy Cauchy--Schwarz, the difference of the two sides is bounded by the\n   816\t\tsquare root of the deficit\n   817\t\t\\[\n   818\t\t\t1 - \\E_{(\\ell,\\ell_X,\\ell_Z) \\sim D}\\\n   819\t\t\t\\E_{(x,z,\\alpha,\\beta) \\in \\ell} \\sum_{a}\n   820\t\t\t\\bra{\\hat\\psi}\n   821\t\t\tT^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z,x}_{a} \\ot\n   822\t\t\t\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},X),x}_{a}\n   823\t\t\t\\ket{\\hat\\psi}\\,,\n   824\t\t\t\\qquad\n   825\t\t\tT^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z,x}_{a}\n   826\t\t\t= \\sum_{f_X,f_Z \\,:\\, f_X(x)=a}\n   827\t\t\tT^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}\\,.\n   828\t\t\\]\n   829\t\tBy the sandwich definition of $T$ and the projectivity of the lines\n   830\t\tmeasurement $\\{\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Line},X),\\ell_X}_{f_X}\\}$, the\n   831\t\tsubtracted expectation equals\n   832\t\t$\\E \\sum_a \\bra{\\hat\\psi}\n   833\t\t\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Line},X),\\ell_X}_{[\\mathrm{eval}_x(\\cdot)=a]} \\ot\n   834\t\t\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},X),x}_{a} \\ket{\\hat\\psi}$,\n   835\t\twhich by Property~2 of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-sublines} is a mixture of the\n   836\t\tcorresponding averages over the restricted distributions\n   837\t\t$D_{\\mathrm{v},i}$. By the error inflation of\n   838\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:restricted-line-mixture-bounds} applied to the\n   839\t\tline--point consistency in item~3 of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-comm-line-cons},\n   840\t\teach restricted term has deficit $O(m\\,\\delta_{\\mathrm{Line}})$, so the\n   841\t\ttotal deficit is $O(m^2\\,\\delta_{\\mathrm{Line}})$ (the final line of the\n   842\t\tsource proof asserts this bound for the consistency term itself rather\n   843\t\tthan for its deficit; see Remark~\\ref{rem:qld-4-13-source-defects}).\n   844\t\tTaking the square root gives the claimed error\n   845\t\t$m\\,\\delta_{\\mathrm{Line}}^{1/2}$.\n   846\t\\end{proof}\n   847\t\n   848\t\\begin{lemma}[The remaining $Z$-point term is close to one]\n   849\t\t\\label{lem:claim-17-3}\n   850\t\t% claim:17-3 in the paper; the original label is recorded here as a\n   851\t\t% comment for cross-reference fidelity.\n   852\t\t\\uses{lem:qld-sublines, lem:qld-xz-lines, lem:qld-4-10,\n   853\t\t\tdef:expanded-point-measurement, def:expanded-state}\n   854\t\t\\[\n   855\t\t\t\\E_{(\\ell,\\ell_X,\\ell_Z) \\sim D}\\\n   856\t\t\t\\E_{(x,z,\\alpha,\\beta) \\in \\ell}\n   857\t\t\t\\sum_{f_X,f_Z} \\bra{\\hat\\psi}\n   858\t\t\t\\big(T^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}\\big)_{\\mathsf{A}\\mathsf{A}'} \\ot\n   859\t\t\t\\big(\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},Z),z}_{f_Z(z)}\n   860\t\t\t\\big)_{\\mathsf{B}\\mathsf{A}''}\n   861\t\t\t\\ket{\\hat\\psi}\n   862\t\t\t\\ \\approx_{\\sqrt{m}\\,(\\delta_P^{1/4} + \\delta_Q^{1/4} +\n   863\t\t\t\t\\eps^{1/4})}\\ 1\\,.\n   864\t\t\\]\n   865\t\\end{lemma}\n   866\t\\begin{proof}\n   867\t\t\\uses{lem:restricted-line-mixture-bounds, lem:qld-sublines,\n   868\t\t\tlem:qld-xz-lines, lem:qld-4-10, lem:qld-comm-cons,\n   869\t\t\tdef:ith-restricted-line}\n   870\t\tBy Cauchy--Schwarz it suffices to bound the deficit\n   871\t\t$1 - \\E \\sum_b \\bra{\\hat\\psi} T^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z,z}_{b} \\ot\n   872\t\t\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},Z),z}_{b} \\ket{\\hat\\psi}$,\n   873\t\twhere\n   874\t\t$T^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z,z}_{b}\n   875\t\t= \\sum_{f_X} T^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z}_{f_X,[\\mathrm{eval}_z(\\cdot)=b]}$.\n   876\t\tBy Property~2 of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-sublines}, the expectation can be\n   877\t\trewritten over the mixture of product distributions\n   878\t\t$D_{\\mathrm{v},i} \\times D_{\\mathrm{v},j}$ with $z$ uniformly random on\n   879\t\t$\\ell_Z$, and, since\n   880\t\t$T^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z,z}_{b}\n   881\t\t= \\E_{x \\in \\ell_X} \\sum_a\n   882\t\tT^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z}\n   883\t\t_{[\\mathrm{eval}_x(\\cdot)=a,\\ \\mathrm{eval}_z(\\cdot)=b]}$,\n   884\t\tone may additionally average over $x$ uniformly random on $\\ell_X$. Up\n   885\t\tto error $m(\\sqrt{\\delta_P} + \\sqrt{\\delta_Q})$ --- obtained by\n   886\t\tapplying the error inflation of\n   887\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:restricted-line-mixture-bounds} to the conclusion of\n   888\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines} (transported to the sub-line distribution\n   889\t\tvia Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-sublines}) and to the consistency relations of\n   890\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-10} --- the resulting quantity is close to\n   891\t\t$\\E \\sum_{a,b} \\bra{\\hat\\psi}\n   892\t\t\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},X),x}_{a}\n   893\t\t\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},Z),z}_{b} \\ot\n   894\t\t\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},Z),z}_{b} \\ket{\\hat\\psi}$,\n   895\t\twhich, since $\\{\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},X),x}_{a}\\}$ is a measurement,\n   896\t\tequals\n   897\t\t$\\sum_b \\bra{\\hat\\psi} \\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},Z),z}_{b} \\ot\n   898\t\t\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},Z),z}_{b} \\ket{\\hat\\psi}\n   899\t\t\\ge 1 - \\sqrt{\\eps}$\n   900\t\tby the self-consistency of the points measurements\n   901\t\t(Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-comm-cons}). The deficit is therefore\n   902\t\t$O(m(\\sqrt{\\delta_P} + \\sqrt{\\delta_Q}) + \\sqrt{\\eps})$, and taking the\n   903\t\tsquare root gives the claim.\n   904\t\\end{proof}\n   905\t\n   906\t\\begin{proof}[Proof of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}]\n   907\t\t\\proves{lem:qld-4-13}\n   908\t\t\\uses{lem:qld-xz-lines, lem:qld-sublines, def:combine-map,\n   909\t\t\tlem:qld-4-12, lem:claim-17-1, lem:claim-17-2, lem:claim-17-3}\n   910\t\tLet $D$ be the distribution of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-sublines} and let\n   911\t\t$D_{|\\ell}$ denote $D$ conditioned on the first element being $\\ell$.\n   912\t\tFor every line $\\ell$ in $\\F_q^{2m+2}$ and $f \\in \\deg_{md+1}(\\ell)$\n   913\t\tdefine\n   914\t\t\\[\n   915\t\t\t\\hat{Q}^{\\ell}_{f}\n   916\t\t\t= \\E_{(\\ell_X,\\ell_Z) \\sim D_{|\\ell}}\n   917\t\t\t\\sum_{\\substack{f_X \\in \\deg_{md}(\\ell_X),\\\n   918\t\t\t\tf_Z \\in \\deg_{md}(\\ell_Z):\\\\\n   919\t\t\t\tf = \\mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}}}\n   920\t\t\tT^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}\\,,\n   921\t\t\\]\n   922\t\ta valid POVM; the polynomial $\\mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}$ of\n   923\t\tDefinition~\\ref{def:combine-map} is well defined here because Property~2\n   924\t\tof Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-sublines} guarantees that $\\ell_X$ and $\\ell_Z$\n   925\t\tare compatible with $\\ell$. If $\\ell$ is axis-parallel, then by\n   926\t\tProperty~3 of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-sublines} so are $\\ell_X$ and\n   927\t\t$\\ell_Z$, hence $f_X, f_Z \\in \\deg_d$ by Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines};\n   928\t\talong such a line either $(\\alpha,\\beta)$ is constant, in which case\n   929\t\t$f = \\mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}$ is a fixed linear combination of\n   930\t\tpolynomials of degree at most $d$, or $(x,z)$ is constant, in which case\n   931\t\t$f$ is affine in the line parameter, so in either case\n   932\t\t$f \\in \\deg_d(\\ell)$. Chaining Lemmas~\\ref{lem:claim-17-1},\n   933\t\t\\ref{lem:claim-17-2} and~\\ref{lem:claim-17-3} with the triangle\n   934\t\tinequality for scalars gives the consistency bound\n   935\t\t\\begin{equation}\n   936\t\t\t\\label{eq:qld-combined-lines-consistency}\n   937\t\t\t\\E_{(\\ell,\\ell_X,\\ell_Z) \\sim D}\\\n   938\t\t\t\\E_{(x,z,\\alpha,\\beta) \\in \\ell}\n   939\t\t\t\\sum_{f_X,f_Z} \\bra{\\hat\\psi}\n   940\t\t\t\\big(T^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}\\big)_{\\mathsf{A}\\mathsf{A}'} \\ot\n   941\t\t\t\\big(\\Id - \\hat{Q}^{x,z}_{f_X(x),f_Z(z)}\n   942\t\t\t\\big)_{\\mathsf{B}\\mathsf{A}''}\n   943\t\t\t\\ket{\\hat\\psi}\n   944\t\t\t= O\\big(m\\,(\\eps^{1/4} + \\delta_P^{1/4} + \\delta_Q^{1/4}\n   945\t\t\t+ \\delta_{\\mathrm{Line}}^{1/2})\\big)\\,;\n   946\t\t\\end{equation}\n   947\t\tsince\n   948\t\t$\\delta_P = \\poly(\\eps, md/q)$, $\\delta_Q = \\poly(\\eps)$, and\n   949\t\t$\\delta_{\\mathrm{Line}} = \\poly(\\eps)$, the right-hand side is a\n   950\t\tfunction of the form $m \\cdot \\poly(\\eps, md/q)$, and\n   951\t\t$\\delta_{\\mathrm{combine}}$ is taken to be such a function dominating\n   952\t\tit. (The source states a second bound for the same quantity, whose\n   953\t\tderivation is not supported by the properties proved for the sub-line\n   954\t\tdistribution; see Remark~\\ref{rem:qld-4-13-source-defects}.) Now\n   955\t\tif the pair $(f_X, f_Z)$ evaluates to $(a, b)$ at $(x, z)$, then\n   956\t\t$\\mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}$ evaluates to $\\alpha a + \\beta b$ at\n   957\t\t$(x, z, \\alpha, \\beta)$; hence the consistency of $T$ with\n   958\t\t$\\hat{Q}^{x,z}$ along the sub-line pairs expressed by\n   959\t\t\\eqref{eq:qld-combined-lines-consistency}, the definition of\n   960\t\t$\\hat{Q}^{\\ell}$ as the image of $T$ under the combining map, and the\n   961\t\tconstruction of $\\hat{Q}^{x,z,\\alpha,\\beta}$ in\n   962\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-12} as the corresponding coarse-graining of\n   963\t\t$\\hat{Q}^{x,z}$ together yield the first relation of\n   964\t\t\\eqref{eq:qld-4-13}. The second relation follows from the analogous\n   965\t\targument with the registers swapped.\n   966\t\\end{proof}\n   967\t\n   968\t\\begin{remark}[Two error routes in the source proof of\n   969\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}]\n   970\t\t\\label{rem:qld-4-13-source-defects}\n   971\t\tThe source proof in \\cite{Ji2020MIPStar} states two different bounds for\n   972\t\tthe quantity \\eqref{eq:qld-combined-lines-consistency}:\n   973\t\t$O(m(\\eps^{1/4} + \\delta_P^{1/4} + \\delta_Q^{1/4} +\n   974\t\t\\delta_{\\mathrm{Line}}^{1/2}))$, obtained by chaining the three claims\n   975\t\t(Lemmas~\\ref{lem:claim-17-1}--\\ref{lem:claim-17-3}), and\n   976\t\t$O(m^2 \\delta_P)$, obtained by decomposing the left-hand side of\n   977\t\t\\eqref{eq:qld-combined-lines-consistency} into restricted-distribution\n   978\t\tterms and bounding each by \\eqref{eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted}; a\n   979\t\tsentence is also duplicated at the corresponding point of the source,\n   980\t\tthe second copy with a malformed reference. The second route requires\n   981\t\tthe joint law of the pair $((\\ell_X, x), (\\ell_Z, z))$, for\n   982\t\t$(\\ell, \\ell_X, \\ell_Z) \\sim D$ and $(x,z,\\alpha,\\beta)$ uniform on\n   983\t\t$\\ell$, to be a mixture of the product distributions\n   984\t\t$D_{\\mathrm{v}_1,i} \\times D_{\\mathrm{v}_2,j}$, since\n   985\t\t\\eqref{eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted} averages over two independently\n   986\t\tsampled line-point pairs; Property~2 of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-sublines}\n   987\t\tdetermines only the two marginal laws of $(\\ell_X, \\ell_Z, x)$ and of\n   988\t\t$(\\ell_X, \\ell_Z, z)$ separately, not the joint law of\n   989\t\t$((\\ell_X, x), (\\ell_Z, z))$, so the decomposition invoked by the\n   990\t\tsource is not established there. The proof above therefore uses only\n   991\t\tthe first route. Neither route, moreover, delivers the error form\n   992\t\t$\\poly(m^2\\eps, md/q)$ claimed in the source. The first route proves\n   993\t\tthe bound $O(m(\\eps^{1/4} + \\delta_P^{1/4} + \\delta_Q^{1/4} +\n   994\t\t\\delta_{\\mathrm{Line}}^{1/2}))$, a function of the form\n   995\t\t$m \\cdot \\poly(\\eps, md/q)$, and no function of $m^2\\eps$ and $md/q$\n   996\t\talone that vanishes as its arguments vanish dominates it: at\n   997\t\t$\\eps = m^{-4}$, and with $q$ taken large, both $m^2\\eps$ and $md/q$\n   998\t\ttend to $0$ while the term $m\\,\\eps^{1/4} = 1$ does not, so the\n   999\t\tderivation does not support the claimed form. Even granting the\n  1000\t\tdecomposition required by the second route, the bound obtained there\n  1001\t\tis $O(m^2\\delta_P) = m^2 \\cdot \\poly(\\eps, md/q)$, which again carries\n  1002\t\ta separate prefactor polynomial in $m$. The statement of\n  1003\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13} above accordingly records the error as\n  1004\t\t$m \\cdot \\poly(\\eps, md/q)$; this form suffices for\n  1005\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-7}, whose error function absorbs the prefactor\n  1006\t\t$m$ into $(md)^a$. In addition, the final line of\n  1007\t\tthe source proof of Lemma~\\ref{lem:claim-17-2} asserts the bound\n  1008\t\t$O(m^2\\delta_{\\mathrm{Line}})$ for a consistency term that is close to\n  1009\t\tone rather than for its deficit; the statements and sketches above\n  1010\t\trecord the corrected assertions.\n  1011\t\\end{remark}\n  1012\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
