 the POVM {sum_{a : f(a)=b} M_a}_{b in beta},\n786-+% including the zero value on b outside the image of f (empty fiber sum). The indexing by\n--\n788-+% the special case where f is a coordinate projection. Verified against the Lean source\n789-+% on 2026-08-30; decidable-equality instance arguments encode no extra hypothesis over\n790-+% the stated finiteness.\n791-+\\begin{definition}[Bracket notation for post-processed measurements]\\label{def:bracket}\n792:+\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement.postprocess}\n793-+\t\\leanok\n794-+\t\\uses{def:povm-conventions, def:post-processing}\n795-+\tLet $\\mathcal A$ and $\\mathcal B$ be finite sets, let $\\{M^x_a\\}_{a \\in \\mathcal A}$ be a family of POVMs indexed by $x \\in \\mathcal X$, and let $f \\colon \\mathcal A \\to \\mathcal B$ be an arbitrary function. We write $\\bigl\\{ M^x_{[f(\\cdot)=b]} \\bigr\\}$ for the POVM derived from $\\{M^x_a\\}$ by applying the function $f$ to the outcome before returning it:\n796-+\t\\[\n--\n1867-+\t\t% The source phrases the next property as: the marginal over\n1868-+\t\t% (ell_X, ell_Z) is \"a mixture of the product distributions\n1869-+\t\t% D_{ALine,i} x D_{ALine,j} and D_{DLine,i} x D_{DLine,j}\". Those\n1870-+\t\t% products are distributions over pairs of line-point pairs, not\n1871:+\t\t% over pairs of lines, so the phrase does not type-check as\n1872-+\t\t% written; the formulation below states the mixture at the level\n1873-+\t\t% of the joint law of (ell_X, ell_Z, u), which is what the proofs\n1874-+\t\t% of lem:claim-17-2 and lem:claim-17-3 use.\n1875-+\t\t\\item For any point of the form $u = (u_X, u_Z, \\alpha, \\beta)$\n--\n2575-+\t\\end{equation}\n2576-+\tthe sum ranging over $g \\in \\mathrm{ideg}_{d,m}(\\F_q)$. If $\\hat{S}^W_g$ is viewed as an operator acting on registers $\\mathrm{A}\\mathrm{A}'$ (resp.\\ $\\mathrm{B}\\mathrm{B}'$), then $\\tilde{M}^{W,\\tilde{u}}_a$ acts on registers $\\mathrm{A}\\mathrm{A}'\\mathrm{A}''$ (resp.\\ $\\mathrm{B}\\mathrm{B}'\\mathrm{B}''$), the $\\tau^W$ factor acting on $\\mathrm{A}''$ (resp.\\ $\\mathrm{B}''$). Each family $\\{\\tilde{M}^{W,\\tilde{u}}_a\\}_{a \\in \\F_q}$ is a projective measurement, because the $\\hat{S}^W_g$ and the $\\tau^W$ projectors are projective and, for each $g$, the projectors $\\tau^W_{(\\mathrm{Dec}(g)\\cdot\\tilde{u})-a}(\\tilde{u})$ sum to the identity as $a$ ranges over $\\F_q$.\n2577-+\\end{definition}\n2578-+\n2579:+\\begin{definition}[Pulled-apart Pauli observables]\\label{def:tilde-w-observables}\n2580-+\t\\uses{def:tilde-m-measurement, def:dual-self-dual-normal-basis, def:subfield-trace}\n2581-+\tLet $\\{e_j\\}_{j \\in \\{1,\\ldots,t\\}}$ be the self-dual basis for $\\F_q$ over $\\F_2$ of Definition~\\ref{def:dual-self-dual-normal-basis}, and let $\\tr = \\tr_{q \\to 2} \\colon \\F_q \\to \\F_2$ be the subfield trace. For all $W \\in \\{X,Z\\}$, $\\tilde{u} \\in \\F_q^M$, and $j \\in \\{1,\\ldots,t\\}$ define the operator\n2582-+\t\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:def-tildewj}\n2583-+\t\t\\tilde{W}^j(\\tilde{u}) = \\sum_{a \\in \\F_q} (-1)^{\\tr(e_j a)} \\, \\tilde{M}_a^{W,\\tilde{u}}\\;,\n--\n2587-+\n2588-+% In the source the following properties are stated inline with the\n2589-+% definition of the observables; they are recorded here as a lemma.\n2590-+\\begin{lemma}[Product form and Pauli relations of the pulled-apart observables]\\label{lem:tildew-product-form}\n2591:+\t\\uses{def:tilde-w-observables, def:s-w-marginals, def:generalized-pauli, def:decoding-map, lem:qld-4-7}\n2592-+\tLet $\\tau^W(\\cdot)$ denote the generalized Pauli $W$ observable (Definition~\\ref{def:generalized-pauli}). For all $W \\in \\{X,Z\\}$, $\\tilde{u} \\in \\F_q^M$, and $j \\in \\{1,\\ldots,t\\}$,\n2593-+\t\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:tildewj-product-form}\n2594-+\t\t\\tilde{W}^j(\\tilde{u})\n2595-+\t\t= \\Big( \\sum_{g_X,g_Z} (-1)^{\\tr(e_j (\\mathrm{Dec}(g_W) \\cdot \\tilde{u}))} \\, \\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z} \\Big) \\ot \\tau^W(e_j \\tilde{u})\\;,\n--\n2617-+\n2618-+The next lemma shows that the pulled-apart measurements are consistent with the original points measurements of the strategy, and self-consistent. In its statement, and for the remainder of the chapter, $\\delta_S$ denotes the function of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-7}, enlarged by an adjustment of the universal constants $a$ and $b$ so as to also dominate additional error terms of order $\\sqrt{\\eps}$, $\\eps$, and $md/q$ that the source absorbs into $\\delta_S$ along the way; such an adjustment is possible since, after shrinking $b$ to at most $1/2$, the term $\\eps^b$ dominates $\\sqrt{\\eps}$ and $\\eps$ for $\\eps \\leq 1$, while $(md)^a q^{-b}$ dominates $md/q$.\n2619-+\n2620-+\\begin{lemma}[Consistency and self-consistency of the pulled-apart measurements]\\label{lem:qld-construct-the-paulis}\n2621:+\t\\uses{def:tilde-m-measurement, def:tilde-w-observables, def:projective-strategy-setup, def:expanded-state, def:consistency, def:povm-distance, lem:qld-4-7, def:indicator-vector}\n2622-+\tThe measurements $\\{\\tilde{M}^{W,\\tilde{u}}_a\\}_{a \\in \\F_q}$ and observables $\\tilde{W}^j(\\tilde{u})$ satisfy the following properties.\n2623-+\t% The paper's statement also quantifies item 1 over j, but j does not occur\n2624-+\t% in item 1; the vacuous quantifier is dropped here.\n2625-+\t\\begin{enumerate}\n--\n2728-+\n2729-+% In the source the following properties are established inline with the\n2730-+% definition of the swap unitaries; they are recorded here as a lemma.\n2731-+\\begin{lemma}[Unitarity and conjugation action of the swap unitaries]\\label{lem:v-swap-conjugation}\n2732:+\t\\uses{def:v-swap-unitary, def:tilde-w-observables, def:tilde-m-measurement, def:generalized-pauli, def:indicator-vector, def:bracket}\n2733-+\tThe maps $V_{\\mathrm{A}}$ and $V_{\\mathrm{B}}$ of Definition~\\ref{def:v-swap-unitary} are unitaries acting on registers $\\mathrm{A}\\mathrm{A}'\\mathrm{A}''$ and $\\mathrm{B}\\mathrm{B}'\\mathrm{B}''$ respectively, and their conjugation action is exact, as follows. For all $W \\in \\{X,Z\\}$, $j \\in \\{1,\\ldots,t\\}$, and $\\tilde{u} \\in \\F_q^M$,\n2734-+\t\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:v-swap-obs-conjugation}\n2735-+\t\tV_{\\mathrm{A}} \\, \\tilde{W}^j(\\tilde{u}) \\, V_{\\mathrm{A}}^\\dagger = \\Id_{\\mathrm{A}\\mathrm{A}'} \\ot \\bigl( \\tau^W(e_j \\tilde{u}) \\bigr)_{\\mathrm{A}''}\n2736-+\t\t\\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad\n--\n2831-+\t\t\\phi_{\\mathrm{A}} \\, (M^{(\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\\mathrm{A}} \\, \\phi_{\\mathrm{A}}^\\dagger \\approx_{\\delta_{\\mathrm{qld}}} (\\tau^W_h)_{\\mathrm{A}''}\n2832-+\t\t\\qquad \\text{and, by the identical argument,} \\qquad\n2833-+\t\t\\phi_{\\mathrm{B}} \\, (M^{(\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\\mathrm{B}} \\, \\phi_{\\mathrm{B}}^\\dagger \\approx_{\\delta_{\\mathrm{qld}}} (\\tau^W_h)_{\\mathrm{B}''}\\;,\n2834-+\t\\]\n2835:+\twhere the $\\approx$ statements hold with respect to the state $\\ket{\\mathrm{aux}} \\ot \\ket{\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\ot M}$ and the answer summation is over $h \\in \\F_q^M$; the constant implicit in $\\approx_{\\delta_{\\mathrm{qld}}}$ (Definition~\\ref{def:povm-distance}) absorbs the factors accumulated above. This shows that the game $\\mathfrak{G}^{\\mathrm{Pauli}}_{(q,m,d)}$ is a self-test, with robustness $\\delta_{\\mathrm{qld}}(\\eps,m,d,q)$, for the canonical Pauli strategy of Lemma~\\ref{lem:pauli-completeness}. Identifying the registers $\\mathrm{A}\\mathrm{A}'$ with $\\mathrm{A}'$ and $\\mathrm{B}\\mathrm{B}'$ with $\\mathrm{B}'$ matches the statement of Theorem~\\ref{thm:pauli}, in which $\\phi_{\\mathrm{A}}\\colon \\mathcal{H}_{\\mathrm{A}} \\to \\mathcal{H}_{\\mathrm{A}'} \\ot \\mathcal{H}_{\\mathrm{A}''}$. Finally, unpacking the dependence on the parameters $\\eps, m, d, q$, the function $\\delta_{\\mathrm{qld}}(\\eps,m,d,q) = O(\\delta_S^{1/4} + md/q)$ has the form $a(md)^a(\\eps^b + q^{-b} + 2^{-bmd})$ for universal constants $a > 1$ and $0 < b < 1$; see Remark~\\ref{rem:pauli-robustness-form} for the reconciliation of this form with the statement of Theorem~\\ref{thm:pauli}.\n2836-+\\end{proof}\n2837-+\n2838-+\\begin{remark}[Norm conventions in the robustness bound]\\label{rem:pauli-robustness-form}\n2839-+\tThe proof above, following the source, establishes the first conclusion of Theorem~\\ref{thm:pauli} in the squared form $\\| \\phi_{\\mathrm{A}} \\ot \\phi_{\\mathrm{B}} \\ket{\\psi} - \\ket{\\mathrm{aux}} \\ot \\ket{\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\ot M} \\|^2 \\leq \\delta_{\\mathrm{qld}}$, whereas the theorem bounds the unsquared norm by $\\delta_{\\mathrm{qld}}(\\eps,m,d,q)$. The two are reconciled by replacing the exponent $b$ with $b/2$ and enlarging $a$, since the class of functions $a(md)^a(\\eps^b + q^{-b} + 2^{-bmd})$ is closed under square roots up to such adjustments of the universal constants. Similarly, the closing sentence of the source proof asserts constants $a > 1$ and $0 < b < 1$, while Theorem~\\ref{thm:pauli} requires only $a \\geq 1$ and $0 < b < 1$; the former implies the latter.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}

